    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "The two exact one-parameter covers contain at most 2n overlapping generic--generic distance-six edges globally. Combining this with Mattarei's affine quotient-fiber cap and the antipodal quotient-mass theorem gives O_6,25^0+(17/10)O_6,25^A<(17/5)C_M n^(5/3)+(17/5)S_A. Consequently C36' follows from 10K_25^0+17K_25^A+68S_A+68C_M n^(5/3)<=750n^2-255Q_n; uniformly, 25(10K_25^0+17K_25^A)<=12134n^2 suffices without estimating the open disjoint correlation.",
